el."}, {"turn": 22, "text": "Opus 5.5 played H7 and lost 20.1 points. Black's lead went from +12.2 to +32.2, and the engine preferred C2. The 14k's reply at J7 gave back 21.8 immediately, so the swing was undone in a single move."}, {"turn": 40, "text": "After the 14k's B7 lost 31.1 points and put White ahead (-7.9), Opus 5.5 played B8 and lost 32.5. That was its worst move of the game, and Black's lead jumped to +24.6. The engine wanted A4."}, {"turn": 65, "text": "With Black's lead at +24.3, the 14k played D1 and lost 24.2 points, taking the score to +0.0. The engine preferred G2. From here the game was level through the late moves."}, {"turn": 79, "text": "At -1.9 the game was nearly even, and the 14k's G1 lost 85.8 points, taking the score to -87.7. The engine's choice was A6. White's capture count rose from 6 to 40 by the final position, and Opus 5.5 finished off the win by playing the remaining points and passing."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only flood-fills groups and liberties on the pasted board, count.py only tallies area and territory for the current position, and the cat/tail/append to games.md is note-keeping; none of them chooses, ranks, or looks ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}